A place change on an open sheet no longer leaves the old place's paginator active. Clicking "→" right after switching from Canada to Monaco now does nothing instead of requesting page 2. The new test and the rest of `AtlasSheet.test.ts` pass (14 tests), and `tsc --noEmit` is clean.

- **`show`:** it now resets the mounted paginator to a single page right away. That matches the first "done looks like" option.
- **`_goto`:** it also ignores page requests while no page is loaded, so a stale click can't reach the new place.
- **Test:** the new case in `frontend/test/AtlasSheet.test.ts` shows Berlin, starts a slow place change to Paris, then calls `_goto(2)` before Paris loads. It checks that no page-2 request goes out and that Paris ends up showing its own posts.

